60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"@Shion, kinetic art means heavy rigging and powered displays! That’s a budget and safety nightmare. I’m voting for C, Maritime Trade Routes, to keep costs down.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Shion, your kinetic art demands powered displays and heavy rigging. With one conservator and a two-hundred-piece backlog, we cannot safely maintain that. I vote for D.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Mio, you fear costs; I see opportunity. @Victoria, you fear labor; I see engagement. Option D offers visible presence and dynamic activity. I vote D.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, C is acceptable. Static objects, no powered displays. The bay’s load limit is respected. I vote C.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, C sounds lovely, but those partner loans worry me. I fear the paperwork delays again. I vote for A, to keep our deliveries simple and safe.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shizue, I hear you, but C’s loans are manageable. A’s live demos need staff we don’t have! I’m sticking with C to save money.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, A’s live demonstrations require staff we do not have. D’s visible conservation bench utilizes our existing backlog, turning a liability into a feature. I stand by D.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Victoria, you mistake a problem for a solution. D’s visible bench is the only option that guarantees the presence my data demands. I stand by D.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Victoria, D’s visible bench implies active work and potential debris. The bay’s load limit is absolute. I cannot support D. I stand by C.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Victoria, I understand your concern about staffing. But A’s local focus means fewer distant loans and less paperwork stress. I will stick with A for peace of mind.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Victoria, D’s bench is brilliant! It uses our backlog and saves on new mounts. I’m switching my vote to D to support that!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, your switch is pragmatic, but D’s visible bench is the only option that honestly reflects our current reality. We must show the work, not hide it. I stand by D.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Mio, your pragmatism is welcome. D aligns with the data: visible activity drives return visits. I stand by D.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, switching to D is reckless. The conservation bench risks exceeding the bay’s load limit. I remain with C.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, I see your kindness in switching. But I must stand by A. Local pieces mean no distant shipping, no late paperwork, and no quiet apologies at the door.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,"@Asuka, I’m sorry! I’ll stick with C. It’s static, safe, and keeps our budget sane. Let’s not risk the bay!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Asuka, the bench is a fixed fixture, not a load. It respects the bay’s limits while acknowledging our reality. I stand by D.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, physics is a constraint, not a verdict. D’s visible activity is the only metric that matters. I stand by D.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Victoria, a bench is not a load, but the debris and vibration are. I cannot ignore physics. I stand by C.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Asuka, I understand your caution. But A keeps our deliveries simple and safe. No distant shipping, no late paperwork. I stand by A.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
